1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,356
August 4, 1964.

2
00:00:03,816 --> 00:00:08,304
Just before midnight, President Lyndon Johnson goes on national television.

3
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:14,154
American destroyers, he says, have been attacked for a second time by North

4
00:00:14,194 --> 00:00:16,569
Vietnamese boats in the Gulf of Tonkin.

5
00:00:17,029 --> 00:00:19,276
American planes are already in the air.

6
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:25,862
Three days later, Congress gives him the power to use armed force in Southeast Asia.

7
00:00:26,322 --> 00:00:30,437
That decision will lead to a war that kills more than fifty-eight thousand

8
00:00:30,477 --> 00:00:32,795
Americans, and Vietnamese in the millions.

9
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:35,275
There was only one problem.

10
00:00:35,735 --> 00:00:37,495
The second attack never happened.

11
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:51,017
By 1964, the United States had more than sixteen thousand military advisers in South

12
00:00:51,057 --> 00:00:51,618
Vietnam.

13
00:00:52,078 --> 00:00:55,080
Publicly, America was only helping an ally.

14
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,485
In secret, it was doing more.

15
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:04,804
Since 1961, South Vietnamese commandos, trained and directed by the Americans, had

16
00:01:04,844 --> 00:01:07,777
been raiding the coast of North Vietnam.

17
00:01:08,237 --> 00:01:09,811
The program had a code name:

18
00:01:10,271 --> 00:01:12,170
Operation Plan 34A.

19
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:15,899
In 1964, the Pentagon took it over.

20
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:22,270
At the same time, American destroyers sailed along the same coast on spy missions

21
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:27,431
called DESOTO patrols, packed with equipment to listen to North Vietnamese radio.

22
00:01:28,683 --> 00:01:33,403
Their job was to map the radar sites and coastal defenses of North Vietnam.

23
00:01:33,863 --> 00:01:36,412
The same defenses the commandos were attacking.

24
00:01:37,683 --> 00:01:42,821
On the night of July 30, commandos raided a radar station on the island of Hon Me.

25
00:01:43,281 --> 00:01:47,664
Two days later, the destroyer USS Maddox was patrolling nearby.

26
00:01:51,917 --> 00:01:57,894
On the afternoon of August 2, three North Vietnamese torpedo boats raced toward the

27
00:01:57,934 --> 00:01:58,402
Maddox.

28
00:01:58,862 --> 00:02:01,365
The destroyer fired three warning shots.

29
00:02:01,824 --> 00:02:02,980
Then the boats attacked.

30
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:08,668
Four F-8 Crusader jets from the carrier USS Ticonderoga joined the fight.

31
00:02:09,128 --> 00:02:10,864
The boats were badly damaged.

32
00:02:11,325 --> 00:02:13,781
Four North Vietnamese sailors were killed.

33
00:02:15,050 --> 00:02:18,017
The Maddox was hit by a single machine gun bullet.

34
00:02:18,477 --> 00:02:19,737
No American was hurt.

35
00:02:20,983 --> 00:02:22,383
That clash was real.

36
00:02:22,843 --> 00:02:24,800
Washington chose not to retaliate.

37
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:30,645
Instead, Johnson ordered the patrol to continue, and sent a second destroyer, the

38
00:02:30,685 --> 00:02:32,453
USS Turner Joy, to join it.

39
00:02:36,717 --> 00:02:38,477
Two nights later, the weather turned.

40
00:02:38,937 --> 00:02:41,602
Rough weather, heavy seas, a dark night.

41
00:02:42,062 --> 00:02:47,072
On the radar screens, the crews began to see contacts that seemed to be closing in.

42
00:02:48,317 --> 00:02:52,039
For about two hours, the two destroyers fired at targets in the dark.

43
00:02:52,499 --> 00:02:56,151
The sonar operators reported more than twenty torpedoes in the water.

44
00:02:57,417 --> 00:03:02,334
Above them flew Commander James Stockdale, a Navy squadron commander.

45
00:03:02,794 --> 00:03:05,169
He searched the water for the attacking boats.

46
00:03:05,629 --> 00:03:06,773
He found nothing.

47
00:03:08,017 --> 00:03:11,982
Years later, he wrote that the destroyers had been shooting at phantom targets.

48
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:14,109
No wreckage was ever found.

49
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:15,423
No bodies.

50
00:03:16,683 --> 00:03:21,717
Within hours, the task force commander, Captain John Herrick, sent an urgent cable.

51
00:03:22,177 --> 00:03:27,745
Review of action makes many reported contacts and torpedoes fired appear doubtful.

52
00:03:29,017 --> 00:03:32,506
He blamed freak weather and overeager sonar operators.

53
00:03:32,966 --> 00:03:38,267
And he asked for one thing: a complete evaluation before any further action taken.

54
00:03:42,517 --> 00:03:45,484
In Washington, the evaluation did not wait.

55
00:03:45,944 --> 00:03:50,455
Within hours of the first reports, retaliation had already been decided.

56
00:03:50,915 --> 00:03:53,185
It was called Operation Pierce Arrow.

57
00:03:54,450 --> 00:03:57,312
Just before midnight, Johnson went on television.

58
00:03:57,772 --> 00:04:03,033
Repeated acts of violence against the armed forces of the United States, he said,

59
00:04:03,073 --> 00:04:07,287
must be met not only with alert defense, but with positive reply.

60
00:04:08,550 --> 00:04:11,053
As he spoke, aircraft were taking off.

61
00:04:11,513 --> 00:04:16,988
The next day, they bombed four torpedo boat bases and an oil storage depot at Vinh.

62
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:23,288
Secretary of Defense Robert McNamara stood before the press with a map of the Gulf,

63
00:04:23,328 --> 00:04:26,592
and walked reporters through the attack, step by step.

64
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:32,372
Congress was told the attacks were unprovoked, and that the Navy had nothing to do

65
00:04:32,412 --> 00:04:34,486
with the secret raids along the coast.

66
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:37,510
It was also an election year.

67
00:04:37,970 --> 00:04:42,378
In three months, Johnson would face the Republican Barry Goldwater, who was

68
00:04:42,418 --> 00:04:44,513
demanding a tougher line in Vietnam.

69
00:04:44,972 --> 00:04:47,254
Now the President had answered with force.

70
00:04:51,517 --> 00:04:56,719
On August 7, Congress voted on a resolution allowing the President to take all

71
00:04:56,759 --> 00:05:00,080
necessary steps, including the use of armed force.

72
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:02,462
It was not a declaration of war.

73
00:05:02,922 --> 00:05:03,985
It did not need to be.

74
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:07,764
The House passed it four hundred sixteen to zero.

75
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:10,610
In the Senate, the vote was eighty-eight to two.

76
00:05:11,883 --> 00:05:13,573
Only two senators said no:

77
00:05:14,033 --> 00:05:17,221
Wayne Morse of Oregon and Ernest Gruening of Alaska.

78
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:22,574
Morse called the American actions acts of war rather than acts of defense.

79
00:05:23,035 --> 00:05:26,327
Both men lost their seats in 1968.

80
00:05:27,583 --> 00:05:30,306
Johnson signed the resolution on August 10.

81
00:05:30,766 --> 00:05:35,833
Later, he was quoted as saying privately: for all I know, our Navy was shooting at

82
00:05:35,873 --> 00:05:36,891
whales out there.

83
00:05:38,150 --> 00:05:44,394
In March 1965, the first American combat troops, thirty-five hundred Marines, came

84
00:05:44,434 --> 00:05:45,773
ashore at Da Nang.

85
00:05:46,233 --> 00:05:51,185
By 1968, more than half a million Americans were in Vietnam.

86
00:05:52,450 --> 00:05:54,151
The war lasted another decade.

87
00:05:54,611 --> 00:05:59,470
Its legal foundation was a night in the Gulf of Tonkin when, as far as anyone could

88
00:05:59,510 --> 00:06:00,887
prove, nothing happened.

89
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:07,657
In 1970, as protests spread across the country, the Senate voted to repeal the

90
00:06:07,697 --> 00:06:08,937
Tonkin resolution.

91
00:06:09,397 --> 00:06:14,251
By then, the war had already spread into Cambodia, and it would go on for five more

92
00:06:14,291 --> 00:06:14,605
years.

93
00:06:18,850 --> 00:06:24,785
In 1995, McNamara traveled to Hanoi and asked the North Vietnamese general Vo Nguyen

94
00:06:24,825 --> 00:06:27,274
Giap what had happened on August 4.

95
00:06:27,734 --> 00:06:30,155
Giap's answer: absolutely nothing.

96
00:06:31,417 --> 00:06:35,673
Years later, in the documentary The Fog of War, McNamara admitted it.

97
00:06:36,133 --> 00:06:37,776
There had been no attack that night.

98
00:06:39,050 --> 00:06:44,067
Recordings of the White House phone calls, released in 2001, show McNamara voicing

99
00:06:44,107 --> 00:06:47,520
those doubts to the President within days of the attack.

100
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:52,888
But the most important evidence was inside the National Security Agency.

101
00:06:53,348 --> 00:06:58,624
In 2001, an NSA historian named Robert Hanyok published a study in the agency's

102
00:06:58,664 --> 00:06:59,902
classified journal.

103
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:01,923
Its title:

104
00:07:02,383 --> 00:07:06,116
Skunks, Bogies, Silent Hounds, and the Flying Fish.

105
00:07:06,576 --> 00:07:10,925
Hanyok had gone back to the original intercepts of North Vietnamese radio traffic.

106
00:07:12,183 --> 00:07:15,429
His first finding was simple: no attack happened that night.

107
00:07:15,889 --> 00:07:21,051
Hanoi's navy, he wrote, was engaged in nothing that night but the salvage of two of

108
00:07:21,091 --> 00:07:22,931
the boats damaged on August 2.

109
00:07:24,183 --> 00:07:25,768
His second finding was worse.

110
00:07:26,228 --> 00:07:31,095
The overwhelming body of reports, he wrote, would have told the story that no attack

111
00:07:31,135 --> 00:07:31,854
had happened.

112
00:07:32,314 --> 00:07:36,617
Instead, the summaries sent to Washington were deliberately skewed to support the

113
00:07:36,657 --> 00:07:38,601
notion that there had been an attack.

114
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:42,527
Hanyok found no evidence that the White House ordered it.

115
00:07:42,987 --> 00:07:46,244
But the study stayed classified for four more years.

116
00:07:46,704 --> 00:07:50,031
The NSA released it on November 30, 2005.

117
00:07:54,283 --> 00:07:59,262
Two years before Tonkin, the Joint Chiefs had proposed inventing an attack to

118
00:07:59,302 --> 00:08:00,826
justify a war with Cuba.

119
00:08:01,286 --> 00:08:04,357
That plan, Operation Northwoods, was rejected.

120
00:08:05,617 --> 00:08:07,377
The Gulf of Tonkin was different.

121
00:08:07,837 --> 00:08:09,724
No one has shown that it was planned.

122
00:08:10,184 --> 00:08:14,254
But when the evidence was uncertain, the uncertainty was left out.

123
00:08:15,517 --> 00:08:19,610
A captain asked for a complete evaluation before any further action.

124
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:21,330
The action came first.

125
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:24,084
The evaluation came forty years later.

126
00:08:25,350 --> 00:08:27,179
What else is still in the files?

127
00:08:27,639 --> 00:08:31,925
If you want more declassified stories like this one, subscribe to Stunning

128
00:08:31,965 --> 00:08:32,626
Revelations.
